@*
===========================================================
ORANGE TENDER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
PAGE: Committee Decision

DEVELOPER OWNER: Doulat
MODULE: Top Committee
TRELLO TASK: Committee Decision
TRELLO URL: https://trello.com/c/RtPahsxa

PURPOSE:
A Top Committee member approves or rejects the executive
summary of one round.

BUSINESS ACCESS:
Top Committee member (assigned to the tender)

ROUTE: /TopCommittee/Decisions/Decision/{id?}

FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION:
- POST vote: one CommitteeVote per member per round (unique
  index); check membership + role + round status.
- When 4/4 Approve: CommitteeRound = Approved,
  Tender.AwardedBidId / AwardedAt, Status = Awarded; notify.
- On Reject: round Rejected; Manager prepares a revised
  summary and a new round.

DEPENDENCIES:
CommitteeVotes, CommitteeMembers, CommitteeRounds, Tenders,
Notifications, AuditLogs.

STATUS:
UI SCAFFOLD ONLY — BUSINESS LOGIC NOT IMPLEMENTED.

IMPORTANT:
No majority or 3/4 outcome exists.
===========================================================
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Committee Decision";
    ViewData["WorkspaceSection"] = "Voting";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Cast your vote on the executive summary. Award requires all four approvals.";
}
<partial name="_PageHeader" />
<partial name="_ScaffoldNotice" />

<partial name="_ApprovalTracker" model='"Top Committee"' />

<div class="pg-grid">
<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Approve award", "Approve the recommended supplier for award.", "Records your Approve vote for this round. The award is recorded only when all 4 members approve.", false, false)' />
<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Reject", "Reject the executive summary.", "Records your Reject vote with a reason and returns the summary to the Sourcing Manager. The rejection stays visible.", true, true)' />
</div>

<aside class="pg-note"><strong>Award rule</strong><p>4 of 4 Approve on the same summary version. On success the tender’s AwardedBidId is set — kept separate from the committee’s recommended bid.</p></aside>
